//Dijkstra repeatedly chooses:
The unprocessed node with the smallest known distance.
Then it tries to improve the distances of its neighbors.
This process is called relaxation.



//"Dijkstra's algorithm finds the shortest path from a single source to all other nodes in a weighted graph with non-negative edge weights. 
// I maintain a distance array and initialize the source to zero and all other nodes to infinity. 
// I use a min-priority queue to always process the node with the smallest current distance. 
// For each neighbor, I calculate a new distance through the current node. 
// If this new distance is smaller than the previously known distance, 
// I update it and add the neighbor to the priority queue. 
// This process continues until the queue is empty."

