Time:  O((V + E) log V)
Space: O(V + E)


//why priority queue?
"Dijkstra always needs to process the unprocessed node with the smallest tentative distance. A PriorityQueue, implemented as a min-heap, allows us to efficiently retrieve that node instead of scanning all nodes every time."

And if they ask why not a normal queue?:

"A normal queue follows FIFO order, not distance order. Dijkstra requires the minimum-distance node first, so we use a min-heap PriorityQueue."